## Font
- **Plus Jakarta Sans** (NOT Manrope, NOT Space Grotesk)
- Weights: 400 (Regular), 500 (Medium), 600 (SemiBold), 700 (Bold)
- Bundle as TTF asset or use google_fonts package

## Currency
- **INR (₹)** with en-IN locale formatting (NOT USD)
- Use: `NumberFormat.currency(symbol: '₹', locale: 'en_IN', decimalDigits: 0)`

## Header Pattern (52px — same across all screens)
```
Height: 52px
Left: Emoji avatar (CircleAvatar) → tapping opens Settings bottom sheet
Center: Screen title (Plus Jakarta Sans, semibold)
Right: Action icon (varies per screen)
Border-bottom: 1px solid palette.border
Background: palette.headerBg
```

## Bottom Nav Pattern (from BottomNav.tsx)
```
Height: 56px
Background: palette.navBg with backdrop blur (white theme only)
Border-top: 1px solid palette.border
4 icons: Wallet, Newspaper, GraduationCap, Cloud
Active: white (dark) / #0F172A (light), strokeWidth 2.4
Inactive: rgba(255,255,255,0.38) (dark) / rgba(0,0,0,0.35) (light), strokeWidth 1.8
Active indicator: 4px round dot below icon, spring animation (damping: 28, stiffness: 340)
Tap animation: scale 0.82
```

## Code Style Rules

### Dart/Flutter
- Always use `const` constructors where possible
- Always use `final` for variables that don't change
- Use trailing commas on all argument lists
- Use single quotes for strings
- Never use `print()` — use the `logger` package
- Split widgets into separate files when they exceed ~100 lines
- Use `ConsumerWidget` or `ConsumerStatefulWidget` for Riverpod

### State Management
- One controller per screen (StateNotifier<FeatureState>)
- State classes are immutable with copyWith
- Use `ref.watch()` in build methods, `ref.read()` in callbacks
- Settings state: Riverpod StateNotifier (convert from settingsContext.tsx)

### Theming
- NEVER hardcode colors — always use the palette/theme system
- Create `AppColors` as a `ThemeExtension` so both themes auto-switch
- Access via: `Theme.of(context).extension<AppColors>()!`

### Database (Drift)
- Tables: expenses, categories, banks, news_articles, cloud_files, saved_words, sync_queue
- Use `.watch()` streams for reactive UI updates
- Write operations must also insert into SyncQueue

### Charts (fl_chart)
- Replace recharts AreaChart → fl_chart LineChart with gradient fill
- Replace recharts BarChart → fl_chart BarChart
- Replace recharts PieChart → fl_chart PieChart
- Match colors exactly from the React source

### Animations
- Replace framer-motion `motion.div` → Flutter `AnimatedContainer` or `AnimationController`
- Replace `whileTap={{ scale: 0.82 }}` → `GestureDetector` + `Transform.scale`
- Replace `AnimatePresence` → `AnimatedSwitcher` or custom transitions
- Replace `layoutId` spring animation → `Hero` widget or custom

### LLM Integration
- AI Categorize: POST /api/v1/ai/categorize (keyword rules locally + LLM fallback via backend)
- AI Rephrase: POST /api/v1/ai/rephrase (7 platform outputs)
- AI Coach Correct: POST /api/v1/ai/correct (5 platform × 3 tone matrix)
- AI Dictionary: POST /api/v1/ai/define (word definitions)
- ALL go through backend API → LiteLLM → Provider. Never direct.

## Don't
- Don't use 5 tabs — it's 4 tabs + settings as bottom sheet
- Don't use Manrope font — use Plus Jakarta Sans
- Don't use USD — use INR (₹)
- Don't use purple #4725F4 as primary — the accent is blue #0D59F2
- Don't put Settings as a tab — it's a DraggableScrollableSheet modal
- Don't hardcode colors — use palette system
- Don't call LLM providers directly from Flutter
- Don't use Navigator.push — use GoRouter
- Don't skip the SyncQueue when writing data
